# BuildKit reads `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` in preference to the context-root
# `.dockerignore`, so this scopes the exclusion to THIS build without putting a
# `.dockerignore` at the repo root where it would affect everyone.
#
# The build context is the repo root, so without this a teammate's local `.venv`
# or `node_modules` would be uploaded to the daemon on every build. Nothing here
# changes what lands in the image (the Dockerfile COPYs only `memory/` and
# `app/`); this is purely about not shipping hundreds of MB to the builder.
.git
.venv
venv
node_modules
__pycache__
*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.wrangler
vendor
eval/.cache
eval/runs
eval/data
plan
agents
motion
realtime
deploy/.env
**/.env
**/*.log
